  "L&S General Guidelines\nGeneral Guidelines\n- All courses intended to fulfill major requirements must be taken for letter-graded credit, other than courses listed, which are offered on a Pass/No Pass basis only. Other exceptions to this requirement are noted as applicable.\n- No more than one upper-division course may be used to simultaneously fulfill requirements for a student's major and minor programs.\n- No more than two upper-division courses may be used to simultaneously fulfill requirements for a double major.\n- To maintain status in the major, a minimum grade point average of C (2.0) must be maintained in all work taken in the major.\n- Students are required to complete at least a C (2.00) average in all upper division (or graduate-level) courses that are used to complete requirements for the major."
